      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Figured it out. Turns out one of the steam deck audio devices called \"Echo-Cancel Sink\" was completely muted causing the audio to cease when VRChat initialized the in-game world audio for the first time.\nFix: Switch to desktop mode and make sure your device volumes are set correctly. In particular, reset the \"Echo-Cancel Sink\" back to full volume.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-10-01T20:12:53.070Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Pretty much the title. When I boot the game on the deck, the audio is fine. I can hear the loading sounds and music as usual.\nBut as soon as I get into a world, it just stops all audio, including voices and menu/ui sounds, _including_ steam deck system UI audio.\nI tried spawning into worlds both with (my usual) and without video players to see if it was an AVPro problem, but there was no change.\nI tried the deck on the beta stuff, again no change.\nI checked all in-game audio controls. I checked my system audio settings. I tried with a completely different system audio output device.\nNo change.\nAgain, I can hear audio just fine UNTIL I get into the world. After that, NO audio works until I close the game.",
